{#
  The library-collection configuration form — the Twig counterpart of
  module/Books/view/books/collections/edit.phtml and its fields-partial.phtml.

  Nineteen plain rows in the partial's order, `submit` among them: unlike the role form
  below, this partial renders its own submit button, so the template does not add one.

  **The stylesheet and script are reproduced with the original's broken path**, and that
  is deliberate. fields-partial.phtml appends
  `$this->basePath() . "/gen-selectize-markdown-$lang.js"` — with no `/js/` segment —
  so the laminas page has been requesting a script that 404s. Every other partial in the
  module writes `/js/…`. It is left wrong here because a porting batch has no business
  silently changing which assets a page loads: fixing it would make the ported page load
  a file the original never has, which is a behaviour change hiding inside a diff that
  is supposed to prove there are none. Recorded in BACKLOG instead; the same rule the
  batch-2 template nits were left alone under.

  **The field rows live in `books/_collection-fields.html.twig` now**, shared with the create
  form so that a field cannot be added to one surface and quietly forgotten on the
  other. What stays in this file is what edit.phtml keeps outside its own partial —
  which is not the same set for every entity, and is the detail worth checking before
  moving anything across the boundary.
#}
{% extends 'layout.html.twig' %}

{% block page_stylesheets %}
        <link href="/css/gen-selectize-markdown.css" media="screen" rel="stylesheet" type="text/css">
{% endblock %}

{% block page_scripts %}
        <script src="/gen-selectize-markdown-{{ current_language() }}.js"></script>
{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<h1>{{ translate(page_title) }}</h1>

{{ form_open(form, form_action) }}
{{ include('books/_collection-fields.html.twig') }}
{{ form_close() }}
{% endblock %}
